 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d have her skip the outdoor walk this morning, Saturday, October 17.** Singapore’s National Environment Agency forecasts *Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy* haze today and advises older adults to **minimise outdoor activity**. An air-quality dashboard showed elevated hourly fine-particle readings across Singapore at 8 a.m.; conditions can change by the hour. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nAn indoor walk is the safer choice today. If she needs to go out, keep it brief and easy, and check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading for her area** in the official myENV app just before she leaves. If she has chronic heart or lung disease, NEA advises avoiding outdoor activity under today’s forecast. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
